{"agent_id":"pp3g-TRrm-review-r4-mimo-quick-pass-fail-154-matrix-results-283f","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T04:32:50.461220536Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ed2be289-b151-45eb-9b85-03749f34d822","comment_uuid":"0552c306-cfd5-4121-9fbe-fcd7e129ce9e","author":"pp3g-TRrm-review-r4-mimo-quick-pass-fail-154-matrix-results-283f","content":"## REVIEW R4 VERDICT: PASS\n\n### Assessment Summary\n\n**1. Pass/fail count: 65/67 — MEETS the >=65/67 bar ✓**\n- 65 checks passed, 2 failed (matrix-fixed-harness-235.log)\n- Down from 53/67 (post-harness-fix) and 39/67 (pre-harness-fix)\n- All 14 prior harness-bug classifications from #232 have been fixed\n\n**2. Remaining failures: BOTH are HARNESS ARTIFACTS (not product issues)**\n\nThe2 failures share ONE root cause: row 1 / row 14 row-1.\n\nFinding 1 — `row1: <=3 POSTs` (matrix-fixed-harness-235.log, run-matrix.sh POSTS1 assertion):\n- Server saw 4 POSTs (server-row1.log: POST#1 16:32:57, POST#2 16:33:05, POST#3 16:33:12, POST#4 16:33:15)\n- Fork terminal WARN reports totalPOSTs=3 (client-row1.out: 'retry budget exhausted' attempt=3 totalPOSTs=3 at 16:33:21)\n- The 4th POST arrives 22ms after the fork's stream starts for attempt 3 (16:33:15.439Z stream → 16:33:15.461Z POST#4)\n- Gap between POST#3 and POST#4 is only ~3s (shorter than bodyIdleTimeout=6000ms)\n- The fork's budget-exhausted fires ~6s after POST#4 (consistent with bodyIdleTimeout firing on the 4th POST)\n\nFinding 2 — `row14: row 1 server POSTs=4 <=3 and terminal totalPOSTs=3 == server count`:\n- Same root cause: server=4, terminal totalPOSTs=3, mismatch\n- The row-14 aggregate assertion checks that server POST count matches the terminal totalPOSTs\n\n**Classification: HARNESS ARTIFACT — the AI-SDK has its own retry layer**\n\nEvidence chain:\n1. The fork's retry logic logs exactly 3 attempts (attempt=1, attempt=2, budget-exhausted attempt=3 totalPOSTs=3)\n2. The server sees 4 POSTs — the 4th is invisible to the fork's logging\n3. The timing pattern (4th POST arrives 22ms after stream start, 3s after POST#3) is consistent with the AI-SDK's own `maxRetries` layer firing independently\n4. The `<=3 POSTs` assertion in run-matrix.sh was calibrated to the fork's custom retry budget but does not account for the AI-SDK's separate retry mechanism\n5. All critical error-handling assertions PASS: exit!=0, exit!=124, ERROR surfaced, per-attempt WARN, budget exhausted, totalPOSTs=3, Body read timed out marker\n\n**3. Matrix evidence supports installing the fork binary: YES**\n\nThe matrix demonstrates:\n- Error surfacing works (all hang rows show ERROR + marker)\n- Retry budget is bounded (3 attempts, then budget-exhausted)\n- Exit codes are correct (exit 1, not 124)\n- Healthy rows complete cleanly (rows 4, 5, 6, 7, 10a, 11)\n- Timeout knobs work (row 8 sensitivity test)\n- Turn-level guard works (row 9b Turn stalled)\n- Static acceptance passes (row 16a-e)\n\nThe 4-POST discrepancy is a harness assertion gap, not a product defect. The fork's error handling and retry budget are working correctly.\n\n### Verdict: PASS\n\nThe matrix is clean enough to install. The 2 failures are harness artifacts (assertion doesn't account for AI-SDK's separate retry layer). All critical product behaviors are verified.\n\n**WHY** — the fork's error path, retry budget, and timeout mechanisms are all verified working by the65 passing checks. The 2 failures are both the same harness-level assertion gap (POST count assertion doesn't see the AI-SDK's own retry).\n\n**WHAT** — this verdict is based on: (1) the matrix log (65/67), (2) server-row1.log (4 POSTs), (3) client-row1.out (fork logs totalPOSTs=3), (4) run-matrix.sh (assertion logic), (5) timing analysis of POST/wire events.\n\n**HOW CERTAIN** — evidence-based. The timing pattern (4th POST 22ms after stream start, 3s after POST#3, invisible to fork logging) is strong evidence of a second retry layer. The alternative (fork miscounting) would require the fork to log 'budget exhausted' while still having a pending POST, which contradicts the sequential retry logic.\n\n**WHAT-NOT-TESTED** — I did not verify the AI-SDK's `maxRetries` default value or confirm that the4th POST is definitively from the SDK's retry layer (would require SDK source inspection or debug logging). The classification is inferred from timing patterns and the fork's logging behavior.","created_at":"2026-08-08T04:32:50.454486915Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:IiWbGUSJlYCvcPflh1VMOa8NSrMPxgTmV/HClhgI5Ao","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgd04p9QJD4aNW05Whhx9HJ+DgV/O2ObYVsPoEqIeXsV0AAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAKuDhyJ3xcF/YdA2bkZ90CM8swz/EbR5v+lDl68VoPvY447RtJB/D9uo7iAe/xiVXmunfmeUhKDmynSbleHuQDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:IiWbGUSJlYCvcPflh1VMOa8NSrMPxgTmV/HClhgI5Ao","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgd04p9QJD4aNW05Whhx9HJ+DgV/O2ObYVsPoEqIeXsV0AAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF5T/Yxglw6iEdoIBR4wKEXCi9K/uoWi4Jya8PKLnN8iJdm+0FGu6sSSqLVGC8SNYQ0BghIOQu12vN/YrmdG6wQ="}
